  "term": "ethical conflict",
  "definition": "Ethical conflict is a situation in which a person faces a dilemma between competing duties, so that some breach of duty seems unavoidable and one must choose the lesser violation. In this historical discussion, it also raises the question of whether moral rules are absolute or relative in their application.",
